From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gabriele Cabrini <gabriele@gabrielecabrini.it>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 21:09:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] backport: wpt: Wait for web fonts before measuring in
 Ahem-based testharness tests (#49502)

Upstream 2b94d76a697, which came after Servo 0.8.0, unchanged:

These tests read layout synchronously while the page is parsing, before
the
Ahem web font from /fonts/ahem.css has loaded. Their measurements then
use a
fallback font's metrics, and the results depend on load timing. Run the
measurements after document.fonts.ready so the results are
deterministic.

With the font loaded, every subtest of
block-in-inline-self-collapsing-margin-001.html passes, so its
expectation
file is removed.

Fixes #49500
Fixes #49491
Fixes #49488
Fixes #49487
Fixes #43763

Fork note: with "fonts: Only load @font-face fonts that the page uses",
Ahem is only fetched once text uses it, so on 0.8.0 the table-cell
subtest of first-baseline-block-in-inline-001.html measured a fallback
font and failed. Drop this patch at the first sync onto a release that
contains #49502, where it applies empty.

Validation: the five changed tests, release builds of this sync's stack on Servo 0.8.0, three runs with SpiderMonkey and three with QuickJS: all as expected (96 subtests each), the table-cell subtest of first-baseline-block-in-inline-001.html passes in each, without an expectation; with the stack's previous version of the test it fails 3 of 3 times. On upstream, bisected: the code of "fonts: Only load @font-face fonts that the page uses" on upstream's commits after 0.8.0 fails it until this commit and passes it from this commit on.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; backported unchanged by the agent during the 2026-11-09 sync)
Signed-off-by: Gabriele Cabrini <gabriele@gabrielecabrini.it>
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
